== MECHANISM VERDICT ==
CONFIRMED. The Close button is painted under the system status bar. Its centre (44 dp) is above the
53 dp status-bar inset, so a tap there is consumed by SystemUI and never reaches Flutter — which is
exactly why there is no exception and no log line. Only the bottom 15 dp of the 48 dp button is
actually hittable. The rival "synthetic tap too fast for the recogniser" theory is dead: a 400 ms
held press at the same point opened the notification shade instead of reaching the app.
